  "id": "invisible-displacement",
  "term": "invisible displacement",
  "definition": "Invisible displacement is the hidden movement of an object from one place to another so that its transfer is not directly seen. In studies of object permanence, it refers to testing whether someone understands that the object still exists and can be found after this unseen move.",
